> **wallhack** (plural **wallhacks**)
>
> *(video games)* A patch enabling a player to cheat by modifying the properties of walls, as by making them transparent or nonsolid.

A Layer 3 tunneling tool built for network pivoting in penetration testing scenarios. It establishes a full TUN interface on the entry node, allowing tools to work transparently — no proxy chains, no SOCKS configuration, just standard traffic routed through the tunnel.

## Performance

Built on QUIC and WebSocket transports, both capable of multi-gigabit throughput. Choose a transport based on network constraints — QUIC offers lower latency, while WebSocket works anywhere HTTP is permitted.

{% grid  %}
{% card title="QUIC Transport" icon="wifi" %}
- **Single stream:** 2.9 Gbps
- **2 streams:** 2.9 Gbps
- **4 streams:** 2.5 Gbps
- **Reverse:** 893 Mbps
{% /card %}
{% card title="WebSocket Transport (TLS)" icon="plug" %}
- **Single stream:** 4.3 Gbps
- **2 streams:** 4.0 Gbps
- **4 streams:** 3.8 Gbps
{% /card %}
{% /grid %}

{% callout type="note" %}
Benchmarks measured with iperf3 over isolated network namespaces with veth pairs. Real-world performance varies with network conditions.
{% /callout %}

## Binary Size

Distributed as a single static binary with no runtime dependencies. If the REST API, REPL, or MCP server are not required, the slim build strips them out entirely.

| Target | Default | Slim |
|--------|---------|------|
| Linux x64 (glibc) | 6.05 MB | 4.65 MB |
| Linux x64 (musl, static) | 6.01 MB | 4.63 MB |
| Linux arm64 | 5.34 MB | 4.07 MB |

